<ID>301856249</ID></XREF_LINK></EXPERIMENT_LINK></EXPERIMENT_LINKS><EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTES><EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>GEO Accession</TAG><VALUE>GSM1856249</VALUE></EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTE></EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTES></EXPERIMENT><SUBMISSION alias="GEO: GSE72153" broker_name="GEO" center_name="GEO" submission_comment="submission brokered by GEO" lab_name="" accession="SRA289537"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRA289537</PRIMARY_ID><SUBMITTER_ID namespace="GEO">GEO: GSE72153</SUBMITTER_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SUBMISSION><Organization type="center"><Name abbr="GEO">Gene Expression Omnibus</Name></Organization><STUDY center_name="GEO" alias="GSE72153" accession="SRP062551"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP062551</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioProject" label="primary">PRJNA293208</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSE72153</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_TITLE>Molecular responses and metabolic reset of apple fruit under postharvest low oxygen stress</STUDY_TITLE><STUDY_TYPE existing_study_type="Transcriptome Analysis"/><STUDY_ABSTRACT>In the present work we report data on the application of an integrated approach on apples held under two levels of low oxygen concentrations  throughout  the initial 2 months of  storage, when, in general, strict control of the effects of the extremely low oxygen concentration is  required for a successful DCA performance. Overall design: Examination of 4 different condition. Three replicates per condition</STUDY_ABSTRACT><CENTER_PROJECT_NAME>GSE72153</CENTER_PROJECT_NAME></DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>pubmed</DB><ID>26909091</ID></XREF_LINK></STUDY_LINK></STUDY_LINKS></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="GSM1856249" accession="SRS1038517"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS1038517</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN03998548</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM1856249</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>Sample from Normoxic condition</TITLE><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXON_ID>3750</TAXON_ID><SCIENTIFIC_NAME>Malus domestica</S